passages.text:
//location dock, background barout2
//show mrred
mrred: Hello, and welcome to our island! I'm Mike, and this is my island. I mean it belongs to me, and I personally greet everyone who rents a house from me!

//you meet msgreen
msgreen: Hello, newcomer! I'm Monica, but you can call me Miss Green. As you see, I've taken my colour — I even dress to match.
msgreen: Lucky it suits me. After decades in a white coat, it's not easy to switch. But enough about me. What brought you here?

//background orange house inside
//show mrred
mrred: Here is your house. Food is delivered once a week, on Mondays. If you get tired of the standard meals, come to me at the bar and say what to order. You can just leave a note. You won't be able to call — there's no mobile signal on the island.

//background orange house inside
mrred: They've been offering to put up a tower for ages, but I refuse. I like the atmosphere of my youth. If you need anything — just come and tell me.
mrred: It helps with privacy too.

//background orange house inside
mrred: Yes — they've been offering to put up a tower for ages, but I refuse. I like the atmosphere of my youth. If you need anything — just come and tell me.
mrred: It helps with privacy. And we value that here.

mrred: Good. There's no mystery here — everyone is older, and everyone has a past. You don't always need to dig it up.

mrred: All right, settle in, look around your home, walk the island, write your book, or drop in on someone — make yourself at home. I must go!
//hide mrred

mrred: There's no mystery — everyone is older, and everyone has a past. You don't always need to dig it up.

mrred: All right, settle in, look around your home, walk the island, write your book, or drop in on someone — make yourself at home. I must go!
//hide mrred

//shows the house view again
//new day
I had a wonderful rest. What next?

//background houseblueout
//show mrblue
mrblue: Hello, Mister Orange! How are you? Off for a walk? Care to come in?

//background housegreeninside
//show msgreen

msgreen: Hello — how's the book coming along?

//background bar
//show mrred
mrred: Hello — how are you? How did you sleep? The first night is often unsettling because of the silence.

//background forrest
//show mrblack
mrblack: Hello. I'm Mister Black.

mrblack: Good. I hope it works out.

mrblack: I'll go for a walk — I like walking in this forest; it's peaceful here. I like walking alone.

//return to map

mrblack: Good.

mrblack: I'll go for a walk — I like walking in this forest; it's peaceful here. I like walking alone.

//return to map

//background houseyellowout
//show msyellow

msyellow: Hello — I don't think we've met yet. I'm Miss Yellow.

msyellow: What brought you here?

//background housepurpleout
//show mrpurple

mrpurple: Looks like we've got another writer?

mrpurple: Want to come inside, or shall we walk down to the beach?

//map travel from purple house to beach
//background beach

mrpurple: Tell me — what's your book about?

//background orange house inside
//show mswhite
mswhite: Hello! I don't think we've properly introduced ourselves yet.

mswhite: I'm White. I'm a newcomer like you. I only moved here recently and still can't get used to the isolation.

mswhite: Would you mind if we took a walk? Where would you like to go?

//travel to forest
//background forrest

mswhite: I love walking here. Black and I used to come often.

mswhite: I'm Barbara. I don't like all these nicknames, though in public of course I follow the rule too. But I'd be pleased if you called me Barbara when we're alone.

mswhite: Tell me why you came to the island.

//travel to lighthouse
//background lighthouse

mswhite: I love this view. The endless sea. You look and lose yourself in thought.

mswhite: I'm Barbara. I don't like all these nicknames, though in public of course I follow the rule too.

mswhite: Tell me why you came to the island.

//background orange house inside
//show mrred
mrred: Good morning! I see you like your sleep!

mrred: I have a little tradition — I always throw a party for a new guest. Tomorrow I want to throw one for you. You'll meet anyone you haven't seen yet, if anyone's left.

mrred: Come tomorrow at three — and don't be late!

//background bar
//show mrred
//show msyellow

mrred: (fragment of conversation) I'm not sure that'll help her.

mrred: Oh, hello, Orange! Haven't seen you this morning.

msyellow: Hello.

mrred: I forgot to ask — what do you prefer to drink at the party?

mrred: All right — see you tomorrow, and don't be late!

msyellow: Bye.

//return to map

You walked through the forest — beautiful and peaceful. Many herbs and shrubs grow around that you know nothing about.

You didn't meet a soul the whole walk.

//return to map

//background bar
//at bar msgreen, mrpurple, msyellow, mrblack, mswhite, mrred, mrblue

From afar you hear music. As if there weren't seven people here but seventy — a hum, everyone talking, waiting for you.

mrred: At last! Welcome, Orange, to this party in your honour! We're glad you're on the island. Relax, drink what you like, talk to whoever you want — we're free here.

//background bar
//at bar msyellow, mrblack, mrblue, mrred

mrred: I wasn't sure what you'd like, so I ordered a bit of everything. Everyone helped prepare this morning! It's tradition.

mrblue: Try the beer — very good, Czech. I loved it in my past life!

mrblue: By the way, how's your book? Have you started yet?

//background barout2
//at bar msgreen, mrpurple, mswhite

mswhite: Hello! Glad to see you. It felt so strange organising a party for someone else. I think my welcome party was only a couple of weeks ago.

msgreen: Now you're properly welcome on our island of retirees!

mrpurple: Hope you're enjoying the party?

//background bar
//at bar msyellow, mrblack, mrblue, mrred

mrblack: (nods)
msyellow: Hello! How do you like the party in your honour?

//background houseorangeinside

Well, what a party last night! I didn't expect much, but it was interesting.

Time to get to work!

What's this note under the door?

//letter

The intro ends here. The game is still in development. If you enjoyed it and want to play the full version — leave your email.

//email form
